    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green). The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it now passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the age-band feature so that `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `birthDate` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns a derived `ageBand`.\n\nChanges, each kept in the layer it belongs to:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `birthDate` (ISO date, optional input) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `ageBand` (read-only, `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time, matching the existing pattern for other derived fields.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `birthDate` column with getter/setter and a `toString` entry, mirroring `registrationDate`.\n\n3. **`db/*/schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table across all four DB dialects.\n\n4. **`AgeBandResolver.java`** (new util) \u2014 A small single-responsibility resolver `bandOf(birthDate, asOf)` computing the band via `Period.between(...).getYears()` (`<18` \u2192 MINOR, `18\u201364` \u2192 ADULT, `\u226565` \u2192 SENIOR), returning `null` when either date is absent. This sits alongside the existing `BusinessDayResolver`/`LocalityResolver`.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired an `ageBand` mapping via a `formatAgeBand(owner)` helper that delegates to `AgeBandResolver`, computing the band from the stored `birthDate` against `registrationDate` \u2014 consistent with how `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, etc. are derived. The inbound `birthDate` maps automatically through the existing `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`.\n\nThe test creates an owner with `birthDate=1990-01-01` (registered today, 2026-09-16, age 36) and correctly receives `ageBand=ADULT`.",
